      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test. The main understandability issue is that `array1`/`array2` names don't reveal their roles — `array1` is mutated into the expected reference, `array2` is the input under test. Renaming to `expected`/`actual` makes each line of the assertion self-explanatory.Now I'll run the compile check.The improved test compiled successfully. The only change made was renaming `array1`/`array2` to `expected`/`actual` throughout all nine test methods, making the assertion `assertArrayEquals(expected, ArraySorter.sort(actual))` immediately self-explanatory — `expected` is the reference sorted by `Arrays.sort`, and `actual` is what `ArraySorter.sort` produces from the same input."
